## Review Blocker Remediation

- Previous independent review found that C24 SQLite triggers still accepted contract-invalid refs and obfuscated secrets when inserted through raw SQL.
- Added RED raw-SQL regressions for percent-encoded and double-encoded transcript refs, nested schemes, whitespace, empty artifact paths, leading slash, traversal, backslashes, default-ignorable secret markers, encoded idempotency keys, and encoded payload secret markers.
- Added RED/GREEN regressions for audio policy and wake word payload parity, descriptor immutability, initial voice session state, immutable session facts, current transcript scope, workspace-global voice command idempotency, and raw SQL idle-resume forgery.
- Strengthened migration 15 with payload/column parity triggers, transcript artifact ref shape checks, normalized text guards on audio policies, wake words, voice sessions, transcripts, and commands, command-backed state transitions, and same-workspace/session/run `current_transcript_id` checks.
- The new RED tests failed before the migration fix, then passed after the trigger hardening.

