## Code And Security Review

- Earlier post-fix independent code review reported no blocking/high findings after the idle-resume raw SQL forgery fix.
- Earlier post-fix independent security review reported no blocking/high security findings after descriptor-only audio/provider, Owner writes, `run:read`, `If-Match`, idempotency, SQL parity, append-only facts, current transcript scope, normalized redaction, and live API/UI wiring review.
- A fresh independent-review rerun in this continuation could not start because the platform returned `agent thread limit reached`. This limitation is recorded rather than treated as a new independent pass.
- Local review covered scope isolation, RBAC, idempotency, optimistic concurrency, SQL parameterization, SQLite triggers/foreign keys, append-only transcript/command facts, command-backed session transitions, transcript lifecycle derivation, raw-SQL parity, normalized secret redaction, API/UI live wiring, and no external audio/provider side effects.
- Local scans found no C24 source use of real microphone APIs, audio playback APIs, provider SDK calls, MCP calls, external network side effects, `any`, `@ts-ignore`, `@ts-expect-error`, non-null assertion patterns, or unstaged whitespace errors.

## Remaining Limits

- C24 has no live audio runtime, no voice provider integration, no transcript artifact writer, no voiceprint storage, and no external connector/MCP execution.
- Future live Voice/Jarvis stages need separate consent, sandboxing, provider credential mediation, retention policy, rate limits, and external side-effect receipts.
